# format=FAST
# Navico/Simrad/B&G proprietary NMEA 2000 capture - source-selection probe
# Captured live from a NMEA2000-over-TCP gateway on a mixed instrument network:
#   Simrad NAC-3 autopilot (+rudder/virtual-rudder/pilot-controller roles), Triton2
#   instruments, AP48 controllers, ZEUS SR-16 MFD, Precision-9 compass, SCX-20,
#   WS320/WS310 wind, DST810, B&G H3000/Hercules system, CORTEX, Orca.
# Trimmed to: ISO Address Claim (60928), Product Information (126996), and all
#   manufacturer-proprietary PGNs (0xEF00, 0x1EF00, 0xFF00-0xFFFF, 0x1FF00-0x1FFFF).
# High-rate PGNs 130824 (B&G sailing stream) and 65350 (compass magnetic field)
#   are down-sampled to every 10th frame to keep the file small.
# Includes live data-SOURCE-SELECTION change events: PGN 130840 carries the selected
#   source's full NMEA NAME keyed by data-type id (data[5]); observed types include
#   0x11 rudder-fb, 0x13 position, 0x1b heading, 0x23 depth, 0x24 boat speed,
#   0x2a apparent wind, 0x2b barometer. PGN 130822 carries the same in compact form.
